# Rasaoi Hallucination & Speculation Guard

Agents MUST enforce these rules when changing intent parsing, scoring, pairings, culinary data, nutrition, or experimental infra.

## Core invariants (never regress)

1. **Dish-non-invention** — `pairings.ts` never creates a Best/Booster dish from intent text alone. Source of truth = `restaurants.menu_items` (+ matrix enrich only). See CRS-003, ROE-001, ROE-003, ROE-004.
2. **Carrier vs dish** — Roti/naan/bread alone is never a Best Match for mood/celebration (ROE-003). Carriers may be inferred staples; dishes may not.
3. **Regional integrity** — South Indian kitchens never receive North bank inventions (Dal Tadka, Butter Chicken, …) (ROE-004).
4. **Catalog integrity** — Do not re-seed or invent venues (ROE-005 Mythaai retired).
5. **Intent grounding** — `parse-intent` output MUST pass `_shared/intent-sanitize.ts` (`mergeDietary`, carrier strip, transcript cuisine/dish extract, **`exclude_ingredients` from negation**). Any model router MUST still call `validateAndSanitize` / `sanitizeFilters` after LLM output.
6. **No Healthy cuisine** — “something healthy” elevates purity only; never `filters.cuisine = Healthy` (ROE-007).
7. **Negation hard-exclude (ROE-017)** — “not / no / excluding / without / but not \<ingredient\>” → `filters.exclude_ingredients`; plates and ranking must strip matching dishes.
8. **Catalog plate gate (ROE-017)** — every Best/Clean/Heritage dish must exist on that venue’s `menu_items` or culinary matrix; cuisine-bank invents without catalog ID are dropped.
9. **Honest named-dish miss (ROE-018)** — when a concrete dish Ask has no catalog hit, do not present ~100% as exact-dish success; prefer Closest / No exact dish. Refresh menus via promote — never invent the missing dish onto another kitchen.
## Speculation tiers (nutrition & knowledge)

| Tier | Meaning | Allowed in UI/ranking |
|------|---------|------------------------|
| `verified` | Menu/USDA explicit | Yes |
| `inferred` | Matrix/heuristic/LLM with corroboration | Yes with caveats |
| `speculative` | Unmapped ingredient, Apify-only, LLM guess | Enrich only on **exact** dish key match; never clinical claims |

- Unmapped USDA ingredients → **quarantine**, never invent macros (`nutrition.ts`, `nutritionQuarantine.ts`, `experimental_nutrition_quarantine`).
- Dynamic culinary overlay (`culinaryRuntime.ts`) must **not** fuzzy-match speculative rows across restaurants.
- Apify / menu-sync cron may write speculative knowledge only; promoting to `menu_items` requires explicit promote flags + Lab-equivalent review.

## Automated gates

Before merge / promotion:

- [ ] `npm test` — especially `pairings.test.ts`, `intentSanitize.test.ts`, `experimental.test.ts`
- [x] `npm run experimental:sim` — **GATE PASS** 520 seeds @ 100% (≥98%) on staging branch (heuristic corpus; not a live LLM parse gate)
- [ ] Formal plate soak recorded + stakeholder approve develop merge
- [ ] Impact doc updated when guard surface changes: `docs/ROE-016-hallucination-guard-impact-analysis.md`

## Agent audit checklist (AI / scoring / experimental)

When touching `parse-intent`, `model-router`, `pairings`, `veda`, `glycemic`, `experimental/**`:

1. Confirm dish names on plates still come from menu/matrix, not LLM filters alone.
2. Confirm sanitize path still runs **after** routed LLM call.
3. Confirm static culinary fallback when remote hydrate fails.
4. Confirm no new public SELECT on sensitive telemetry without RPC review.
5. Confirm Apify/webhook paths do not auto-promote speculative rows onto plates.
6. Confirm sweet intent never false-matches via bare tokens like `mysore` on dosa names.
7. Confirm negated ingredients appear in `exclude_ingredients` and are stripped from plates.
8. Document findings in impact analysis §Post-implementation audit.

